A||||4||theogre||Seats. Lacking a good one?||||
Z||000000||theogre||09-09-1999||10:15 PM||||As many of you know, finding a drivers seat in decent shape is next to imposible. But. Did you know you can alter a pasenger side seat? At least most of it.<P>The Back frame of the seat is dificult if not imposible to convert from one side to the other but it's upolstery moves easily. You need only unzip the base and carefully pry off the hog rings the anchor it at various points. Reverse the process to put it on the other seat. The whole thing takes less than 1/2 hour. ((Unless you have major foam damage. That adds some time to the repair.))<P>The bottom of the seat Can be converted WHOLE from one side to the other. First remove the hardware. Then remove the hog rings from the sides and the long back flap.<P>Pull the seat cover off to expose the back half of the frame. There is a large clip nut on the side where the pivot stud was. Move that clip to the other side.<P>Clean out the holes for the hinge bolts. ((Note: these holes are not threaded. The bolts will are self tapping.))<P>Reattach the seat cover to the frame. Ideally use new hog rings, but you can use almost anything reasonably strong like wire ties or steel wire. There is not allot of tension on the anchor points.<P>reattach all the hardware for the drivers side. The hinge bolts are self tappers (thread displacing) you'll want a good size wrench.<P>Yea, you end up with blemishes where the hinge was on one side of the seat bottom but it's up side the hump so who cares. At least you aren't sitting on the foam anymore.<P>If I remember right you can get hog rings from JC Whitless.||||reg||
Z||000001||ChadMan||09-10-1999||08:58 AM||||That's a great tip, Ogre.  The bottom of seat I got from Kick Hill was actually a converted passenger unit.  I was a little sore until I put it in the car and realized it looked and worked just as well as a driver's side seat.||||reg||
Z||000002||ggarsk||09-10-1999||11:19 AM||||Thanks for the tip ogre. I know where there are some pass. seats in good shape. I konw what I'm gonna be doing today. :-)<BR>||||reg||
Z||000003||WisconsinGT||09-10-1999||11:30 AM||||Great tip! I too, received my seat from Kick hill. The seats had three holes on both sides. I was pissed until I attached the bottom to the top of the seat. The grey plasitc cover, covered up the holes. No problem. Also, on the side of the seats where only one bolt goes into the seat. (The side that faces the center.) is there a cover or something that goes over it? The reason I ask is,  I noticed that there is a mark on the carpet that looks like the old seats rubed aginst it, from moving the seats forward and back. Thanks||||reg||
Z||000004||theogre||09-10-1999||01:59 PM||||there is no cover for the inner side. Try pulling the seat toward the door before tightening the nuts on the floor. There's a small amount of adjustment there. It might help, might not.||||reg||
